hadiths[23]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18059","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Uthman narrated to us, Musa ibn Talhah narrated to me that Uthman ibn Abi al-As narrated to him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to lead his people, he said: Then he said: Whoever leads people, let him lighten, for among them are the weak and the old and the sick and the one with a need, then when he prays alone, let him pray as he wishes."
"18060","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Ali ibn Zayd from Abu Nadrah, he said: We came to Uthman ibn Abi al-As on a Friday to present a mushaf of ours against his mushaf, then when Friday came he ordered us, so we washed, then perfume was brought and we perfumed ourselves, then we came to the mosque and sat with a man, then he narrated to us about the Dajjal, then Uthman ibn Abi al-As came, so we stood to him and sat, then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There shall be for the Muslims three garrison cities: a city at the junction of the two seas, and a city at al-Hirah, and a city in Sham. Then the people shall panic three panics, then the Dajjal shall come out among the people, then he shall defeat those from the east. Then the first city he comes to is the city at the junction of the two seas, then its people shall become three groups: a group saying: We shall confront him, we shall see what he is, and a group joining the bedouins, and a group joining the city next to them. And with the Dajjal are seventy thousand wearing sijan, and most of his followers are the Jews and the women. Then he shall come to the city next to it, then its people shall become three groups: a group saying: We shall confront him and see what he is, and a group joining the bedouins, and a group joining the city next to them in the west of Sham. And the Muslims shall withdraw to Aqabat Afiq, then they shall send forth their grazing livestock, then their livestock shall be stricken, then that shall be hard upon them, and severe hunger and severe hardship shall befall them, until one of them burns the string of his bow, then eats it. Then while they are so, a caller shall call at dawn: O people, relief has come to you, three times. Then some of them shall say to others: This is the voice of a satiated man. And Isa ibn Maryam shall descend at the dawn prayer, then his commander shall say to him: Spirit of Allah, advance, pray. Then he shall say: This community are commanders over one another. Then their commander shall advance and pray, then when he has finished his prayer, Isa shall take his spear and go toward the Dajjal, then when the Dajjal sees him he shall melt as lead melts, then he shall place his spear between his collarbone, then kill him, and his companions shall flee. Then there is nothing that day sheltering any of them, until the tree says: O believer, this is a disbeliever, and the stone says: O believer, this is a disbeliever."
"18061","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us from Abu Nadrah, he said: We came to Uthman ibn Abi al-As to present a mushaf of ours against his mushaf, and he mentioned its meaning, except that he said: Then there is nothing that day sheltering any of them, and he said: He melted as lead melts."
"18062","Hashim narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me from Said ibn Abi Hind that Mutarrif, a man from Banu Amir ibn Sasaah, narrated to him that Uthman ibn Abi al-As al-Thaqafi called for milk to give him to drink. Mutarrif said: I am fasting. Then Uthman said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Fasting is a shield from the Fire like the shield of one of you from fighting."
"18063","And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Good fasting, three days of the month."
"18064","Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us from al-Hasan from Uthman ibn Abi al-As from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A caller calls every night at an hour therein: Is there a supplicant, so I respond to him. Is there an asker, so I give him. Is there a seeker of forgiveness, so I forgive him."
"18065","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Said al-Jurayri from Abu al-Ala from Uthman ibn Abi al-As and a woman from Qays that they heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), one of them said: I heard him saying: O Allah, forgive me my sin, my mistake and my intent. O Allah, I seek guidance from You for the most right of my affair, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of myself."
"18066","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Said al-Jurayri from Abu al-Ala from Mutarrif ibn Abdullah that Uthman ibn Abi al-As said: O Messenger of Allah, make me the imam of my people. He said: Follow the weakest of them, and take a caller to prayer who does not take a wage for his call."
"18067","Sulayman al-Hashimi narrated to us, Ismail, meaning Ibn Jafar al-Madini, narrated to us, Yazid, meaning Ibn Khusayfah, informed me from Amr ibn Abdullah ibn Kab al-Sulami that Nafi ibn Jubayr informed him that Uthman ibn Abi al-As came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a pain had seized him that had almost disabled him, then he mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he claimed that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Place your right hand upon the place of you which you complain of, then wipe with it seven times, and say: I seek refuge in the might of Allah and His power from the evil of what I find, in each wiping."
"18068","Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Harrani narrated to us from Ibn Ishaq, meaning Muhammad, from Ubayd Allah, or Ubayd Allah ibn Talhah ibn Kariz, from al-Hasan, he said: Uthman ibn Abi al-As was invited to a circumcision, then he refused to accept, then it was said to him, then he said: We would not attend circumcision in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), nor would we be invited to it."
"18069","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Said al-Jurayri informed us from Abu al-Ala from Mutarrif, he said: I entered upon Uthman ibn Abi al-As, then he ordered for me milk of a milch camel, then I said: I am fasting. Then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Fasting is a shield from the punishment of Allah like the shield of one of you from fighting."
"18070","And good fasting, three days of every month."
"18071","He said: And the last thing the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entrusted to me that he said: Make light in your prayer, and measure the people by the weakest of them, for among them are the small and the old and the weak and the one with a need."
"18072","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us from al-Jurayri from Abu al-Ala from Mutarrif, he said: I entered upon Uthman ibn Abi al-As, and he mentioned its meaning."
"18073","Abd al-Samad and Affan, the meaning, both said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us from al-Hasan that Ibn Amir employed Kilab ibn Umayyah over al-Ubullah, and Uthman ibn Abi al-As in his land, then Uthman came to him and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abd al-Samad in his hadith said saying: Indeed in the night is an hour, the gates of heaven are opened therein, a caller calls: Is there an asker, so I give him. Is there a supplicant, so I respond to him. Is there a seeker of forgiveness, so I forgive him. Both together said: And Dawud went out one night, then he said: No one asks Allah Almighty anything except He gives him, except he be a sorcerer or a tax-collector. Then Kilab called for a small boat, then rode in it and went down to Ibn Amir, then he said: Take your office. He said: Why. He said: Uthman narrated to us such and such."
"18074","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Humayd from al-Hasan from Uthman ibn Abi al-As that the delegation of Thaqif came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he lodged them in the mosque that it be softer to their hearts, then they stipulated upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that they not be conscripted, nor tithed, nor levied, nor anyone other than them be put in authority over them. He said: Then he said: You have that you not be conscripted, nor tithed, nor anyone other than you be put in authority over you."
"18075","And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no good in a religion in which there is no bowing."
"18076","He said: And Uthman ibn Abi al-As said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me the Quran and make me the imam of my people."
"18077","Affan narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Uthman narrated to us from Dawud ibn Abi Asim from Uthman ibn Abi al-As that the last with which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) parted from him, he said: When you pray with people, lighten with them, until he specified for me: Recite in the name of your Lord who created."
"18078","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us from al-Hasan from Uthman ibn Abi al-As that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A caller calls every night: Is there an asker, so I give him. Is there a seeker of forgiveness, so I forgive him. Is there a supplicant, so I respond to him."
"18079","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us from Zaidah from Abdullah ibn Khuthaym, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Asim al-Thaqafi narrated to me from Uthman ibn Abi al-As that the last speech with which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke to me when he employed me over Taif, then he said: Lighten the prayer upon the people, until he specified for me: Recite in the name of your Lord who created, and its likes of the Quran."
"18080","Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Abdullah, meaning Ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yala al-Taifi, narrated to us from Abdullah ibn al-Hakam that he heard Uthman ibn Abi al-As saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) employed me over Taif, and the last that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entrusted to me, he said: Lighten the prayer upon the people."
"18081","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Huraym narrated to us from Layth from Shahr ibn Hawshab from Uthman ibn Abi al-As, he said: I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he raised his gaze, then lowered it until he almost stuck it to the ground, he said: Then he raised his gaze and said: Jibril came to me, peace be upon him, then he commanded me to place this verse in this place of this surah: Indeed Allah commands justice and excellence and giving to the near kin, and forbids shameful and evil and transgression, He admonishes you that you may remember."
